Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||08-22-2000||05:12 PM||||I was sitting in a traffic jam yesterday and when I hit the gas to move forward I noticed a massive amount of exhaust smoke coming out the back of my car.  The car runs fine other than that and I would like any suggestions as to what my problem is.<P>I'm getting a state inspection on the 31st so maybe the garage can help me out.<P>FWIW, I have a 1986 2m4 with 74,000 miles.||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||08-22-2000||05:18 PM||||I'll bet your valve seals are allowing oil to be pulled into the combustion chamber at idle (high vacuum conditions)...when you take off, you get a cloud of whitish blue smoke.<P>Hope that's all it is...hope it isn't head gasket (coolant).<P>If your car smokes when you start it up (blue)...more than likely this is your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slapnutz2000||08-22-2000||06:24 PM||||I'm pretty sure my valve seals are wearing thin. Roughly much would it be to replace the seals and what else should I be looking for to go wrong if I don't repair them right away?<P>I got a new head gasket and valve job done about 2000 miles ago and there isn't any blue smoke coming out of the exhaust so that isn't the problem.<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
